  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_0' aria-label=\" Special Police Establishment versus Kamta Prasad Mishra and Others pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('0','2026','2026_7_113_141','2026INSC644'); ><font size='4'> <strong>SPECIAL POLICE ESTABLISHMENT<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>KAMTA PRASAD MISHRA AND OTHERS </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 7 S.C.R. 113</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2026 INSC 644</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010001922026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : J.K. MAHESHWARI, <sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup></strong><br> Issue for Consideration Issue arose whether the Special Police Establishment-SPE as constituted u/s.2(1) of the Madhya Pradesh Special Police Establishment Act, 1947 for investigating offences specified by the State Government u/s.3 of the Act of 1947 entitled to exemption from Act of 2005 by virtue of s.24(4) thereof, on the ground that it is an &lsquo;intelligence and security&rsquo; organisation; and whether the Notification dated 25.08.2011 provides for a matter beyond the parent legislation or whether it is intra vires s.24(4) of the Act of 2005. Headnotes&dagger;<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 15-06-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CRIMINAL APPEAL No. 3743/2024</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Dismissed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('0','2026','2026_7_113_141','2026INSC644','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='col-aut